  "goodToKnow": "Trompeten means to play the trumpet, to trumpet (of elephants) and figuratively to blare out: Er trompetet seine Meinung in die Welt hinaus. Humorously, it also describes loud nose-blowing. Die Trompete is a trumpet. Because the first syllable isn't stressed, the participle has no ge-: hat trompetet. Bach's cantatas and the Brandenburg Concerto No. 2 feature famous trumpet parts."
